CLAUDE.local.md

# root-clutter scratch artifacts (flagged by the 2026-06 review; the review
# itself is now docs/superseded/CODE_REVIEW.md:88, which is where the finding
# was raised). `_tot.png` needs no entry -- `_*.png` above already covers it.
snip.png
trial-export-rooms.csv

# Screenshots dropped in the root by the Windows snipping tool while testing.
# They are EVIDENCE of a session, not of the project: several are cited by name
# in the progress log (e.g. "Screenshot 2026-08-01 175022.png" in D35's record),
# so they are worth keeping locally and never worth committing. Ignoring the
# class is the only part of this with git value -- the existing files are
# scratch and are left exactly where they are.
Screenshot*.png

# transfer buffer for staging files for deletion — always meant to be empty,
# so it is not part of the project (keeps it out of the tree and the ruff gate)
_to_delete/

# the gate's own verdict, written by tools/gate.py at the end of a full-mode
# run and read by .claude/hooks/verify_gate.py before any commit. It is a fact
# about ONE working tree at ONE moment -- committing it would make a stale
# verdict travel to other machines as though it were current.
.gate-result.json
